            "text": "An efficient implementation in Python that balances memory usage and execution speed using NumPy and block-wise matrix operations:\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n\ndef main():\n    # Load the vectors and cast to float64 to ensure high numerical precision\n    X = np.load(\"vectors_secondary.npy\").astype(np.float64)\n    n = X.shape[0]\n    sq_norm = np.sum(X**2, axis=1)\n\n    total_upper = 0.0\n    block_size = 2000\n\n    # Exploit symmetry: D_ij = D_ji and D_ii = 0.\n    # Total sum over all ordered pairs = 2 * sum_{i < j} D_ij.\n    for i in range(0, n, block_size):\n        X_i = X[i : i + block_size]\n        sq_i = sq_norm[i : i + block_size, None]\n\n        for j in range(i, n, block_size):\n            X_j = X[j : j + block_size]\n            sq_j = sq_norm[j : j + block_size]\n\n            # Compute squared Euclidean distance using ||a - b||^2 = ||a||^2 + ||b||^2 - 2<a, b>\n            gram = X_i @ X_j.T\n            d2 = sq_i + sq_j[None, :] - 2.0 * gram\n            np.maximum(d2, 0.0, out=d2)\n            d = np.sqrt(d2)\n\n            if i == j:\n                total_upper += np.sum(np.triu(d, k=1))\n            else:\n                total_upper += np.sum(d)\n\n    total = 2.0 * total_upper\n    print(f\"TOTAL:{total}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
